After years of on-and-off play, I finally did it.  I think the
key to suriving well in this game was starting with Magic Missile,
and an early bones (only one the whole game) on the second level
of the mines with Magicbane.  I had one scary moment just before
going on the quest when I had a power outage while playing, but
it managed to recover the game ok.

By time I got the castle wand (0:1), I already had speed boots
and SDSM I had enchanted up, I had written a spellbook of identify,
had found and used a couple blessed scrolls of genocide, and really
didn't have a lot left that I really needed, so I just went for
gauntlets of dexterity, helm of brilliance, ring of slow digestion,
a ring of levitation to replace the one I had just lost, and used
the final charge for a spare magic marker.  I never did use either
of my magic lamps, and every throne I sat on immediately vanished
in a puff of logic.

I also decided not to wish for any artifacts unless things got
desperate.  I found Magicbane early in a bones, but didn't find
any more until Trollsbane was sitting in the Castle weapons room.
A baluchitherium, of all things, dropped Snickersnee in Gehennom,
and on my way back up to the Planes, I made Orcrist and Sting at
my stash.  An archon on Astral gave me Demonbane, and other than
the invokation stuff and the Eye of the Aethiopica, that was it.
All my previous characters to reach Gehennom had about twice the
random artifacts appear.

This is only about my fourth character to reach Gehennom, and the
second time I've met Demogorgon.  I was only about two or three
levels below the Valley, fighting a random &, when a purple &
appeared next to it (Yeenoghu) and 2 turns later, a second purple
& (Demogorgon) popped in.  I saved the game there and didn't come
back to it for about 3 weeks.  I used that time to review the
spoilers (many thanks Kate N. for your FAQ), trying to remember
if I had cure sickness or not (I did, at 0%), and went back in
ready.  That was only one of two times I teleported that game
(first was a desperation random teleport from a scroll in minetown),
to put myself back on the upstairs, where I quickly used Magicbane
to engrave Elbereth.  From there, it was relatively easy between
cure sickness, a unihorn to unconfuse me (Yeenoghu was still around
as well), and Magicbane to attack.  When I got the message that I
had killed Demogorgon, I took a second break from the game (about
2 weeks this time) out of sheer relief.

When I came back, I decided I'd try for a complete set of Demon
Lords and Princes, so I let Asmodeus live for quite a long time,
until he had brought in Geryon and Dispater as well.  Many long
wait commands later, I had my full set.  The rest of the game
was pretty much anticlimactic until I reached Air, where those
stupid Air Elementals almost did me in when the potion of full
healing (milky in this game) paralyzed me when the ghost popped
out.  I quickly dashed for the portal, and reached Astral.

Of course, once there, I chose wrong twice, and had to go to the
third altar to get the right one.

